e","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add acceptance-criteria lines covering the feature-branch lifecycle (create/observe-on-mirror/delete on success and failure) and the exit-code taxonomy (GATE-BLOCKED on any -1, HARNESS-FAILURE on prerequisite failure or absent-through-poll labels).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0929,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Original AC: '[ ] The E2E fails unless both LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 are present', '[ ] Submit and GitHub-replication assertions run only after both votes pass'","2026-09-07 adds branch create/observe/delete requirement and 'fail with an explicit harness error naming the branch-replication/cleanup prerequisite'","2026-09-08 adds 'If either label is -1, exit GATE-BLOCKED; if either label is absent through the bounded poll, exit HARNESS-FAILURE'"],"finding":"The original Acceptance Criteria checklist was never amended to cover deliverables introduced by later remediations: the replicated feature-branch lifecycle (create/observe-on-mirror/delete) and the exit-code taxonomy (HARNESS-FAILURE vs GATE-BLOCKED). The owner test asserts branch target and cleanup, but no AC line names these as completion requirements.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd2c42ca473c2b644","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria vs 2026-09-07 re-dispatch and 2026-09-08 remediation","norm_id":"n61b8d36a98b385f1","priority":0.8571,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer working from the AC checklist alone could omit branch-lifecycle cleanup or the exit-code distinction and still consider the ACs satisfied."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix"