.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define concurrency ownership for the shared refs — either a per-run unique branch/ticket name or an explicit single-runner lock — so create/update and cleanup are safe and idempotent under overlapping runs.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.752,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'The script must create/update the temporary feature branch for the run, use that branch as the test change target, and clean it up ... by deleting the temporary feature/e2e-gate-smoke branch/ref'","ABSENCE: no statement of ownership, per-run unique naming/lock, or idempotency under concurrent invocations — a second run's cleanup could delete the first run's live branch (TOCTOU)."],"finding":"The E2E uses a fixed shared branch name (feature/e2e-gate-smoke) and a shared tickets branch with 'create or update' semantics, but ownership/concurrency for overlapping runs is undefined — two runs collide on the same ref (check-then-act on branch create/update, non-idempotent cleanup deleting the other run's branch).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0e4fdda1d619ae15","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan-review re-dispatch 2026-09-07 and remediation 2026-09-08 — 'create/update the temporary feature branch' / 'feature/e2e-gate-smoke'","norm_id":"nc6578fb01d4afc79","priority":0.198,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two operators (or a re-run overlapping a prior run) both target feature/e2e-gate-smoke; one run's cleanup deletes the ref the other run is still waiting on Verified for, producing a spurious HARNESS-FAILURE."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Suffix the temporary branch (and disposable ticket) with a run-unique token (timestamp/uuid) and scope cleanup to that run's own ref, or document that the script requires exclusive execution.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75